  [PASS] both runs have nominally significant tests (3 and 2) and ZERO Holm survivors. Neither published MERGING WINS verdict survives the smallest defensible correction for the family it was selected from -- the smallest p in each run misses the first Holm threshold (0.05/12 = 0.00417) by roughly 5x
  [info] run 13's smallest p in the whole family is M=1920 router on `ned` (p=0.0240), a pair the published recall-only rule scored FLAT (+2.86, CI [-0.30,+6.02]). The pre-registered quantity was the less sensitive one ON THE ROW D13 HEADLINED. Recorded as a reason to distrust that row's null -- NOT as a licence to re-headline on ned, which would be choosing the metric after seeing the data.

